# ChangeLog

Version 1.9 (2026-03-21)

- Fixed crash when switching models (e.g., M100 to T200) caused by improper
    deletion of FLTK-managed menu widgets in T100_Disp destructor. The menu
    button widgets (m_LeftClick, m_LeftClickQuad, m_CopyCut) are managed by FLTK
    and should not be explicitly deleted. Changed destructor to only null out
    pointers instead of calling delete, allowing FLTK to handle cleanup properly.

Version 1.8 (2026-03-21)

- Fixed macOS C++ compile failure in preference handling by using C++-safe
    conversion (`std::atoi`) and proper header usage in `pref_form.cpp`.

- Fixed arm64 link failure in remote processing by replacing legacy
    `fl_wait(double)` usage with FLTK API `Fl::wait(...)` calls.

- Updated build/link flags for Darwin to remove stale/legacy library paths
    (including old X11 and Homebrew libpng path handling) and removed duplicate
    pthread linkage noise in makefiles.

- Performed project-wide `sprintf` to `snprintf` migration across modified
    source files to address modern macOS deprecation warnings.

- Updated FLTK API usage in editor/UI code to newer calls where needed
    (including replacement of deprecated cursor-position methods).

- Corrected memory-management and safety issues found during warning cleanup,
    including mismatched `new[]`/`delete` handling and related warning fixes.

- Resolved additional compiler warnings across C/C++ modules, including
    assignment-in-condition cleanup, prototype modernization, empty-body cleanup,
    logical precedence fixes, and unused/extra argument fixes.

- Added Apple-clang scoped suppression around deprecated `sem_init` usage in
    `m100emu.c` to keep build output clean while preserving behavior.

- Applied related formatting-safe warning cleanups in touched modules such as
    assembler/disassembler, IDE/editor windows, memory tools, socket dialogs,
    printer/paper views, and peripheral/remote support code.

- Verified successful full build after the above changes (`virtualt` and
    `vt_client` binaries produced).

- Current uncommitted workspace also contains generated build/runtime artifacts
    from local builds and execution, including `.dep/`, `obj/`, model
    directories (`M10`, `M100`, `M102`, `T200`, `PC8201`, `PC8300`, `KC85`),
    plus built binaries and `.DS_Store`.


For versions prior to Version 1.8, see [release.txt](./release.txt).
